# CliffT₂ derives the decoded relations of its sources (Appendices D, F.4, G.4)

The derivations of Appendix D, each replayed line by line from the paper's
figures; then, on two wires, the decoding of every relation (C1)–(C20) of
Bian and Selinger's presentation (Appendix G.4, `BS.rel_derivable`) and the
round trips of the generators (Appendix F.4, `BS.DE_gen`); and on one wire
and none the same for Greylyn's relations in dimensions `2` and `1`
(`GL.rel_derivable₁`, `GL.rel_derivable₀`), which the paper does not
treat.  Each step between two printed lines was found by a search over
rewrites modulo commuting gates on disjoint wires, using the rules the paper
cites for that step (and their derived forms), and is replayed by `derive`.
Where the paper's relation differs from Bian and Selinger's statement
((C15) is drawn as (TX), `T X = X T† ω`, where they state `(T X)² = ω`),
the search derives their statement from the rules the paper cites.

Generated by `gen/gen_tcliff.py` from the derivations `gen/run_tcliff.py`
finds (the figures read by `gen/figparse.py`).
-/
